## SiteRM 1.6.2 Release

### 🚀 New Features

**Junos MX/PTX support**
- `SiteFE/ProvisioningService/modules/VirtualSwitchingService.py`, `SiteRMLibs/Backends/Ansible.py`: Added support for Junos MX/PTX virtual-switch mode, which names VLANs on-device as `VLAN-<id>` instead of the standard `Vlan<id>`. Enabled per-host via `ansible_params.vlanmode: mx|ptx`.

**Per-agent DSCP control flag**
- `SiteFE/REST/Host.py`, `SiteRMAgent/Ruler/Ruler.py`, `SiteRMLibs/GitConfig.py`: Added a `nodscp` host flag (alongside the existing `noqos`) to allow disabling DSCP rule application per agent.

**Manual configuration files (bypass GitHub)**
- `SiteRMLibs/ConfigFetcher.py`, `SiteRMLibs/GitConfig.py`: Frontend/Agent main, auth, and auth-refresh configuration can now be supplied from local YAML files instead of a Git repository, via `MAIN_CONFIG_FILE`, `AUTH_CONFIG_FILE`, `AUTH_RE_CONFIG_FILE`, and `MAPPING_TYPE` (env var or `/etc/siterm.yaml`). When `MAIN_CONFIG_FILE` is set, the Git fetch/mapping lookup is skipped entirely.

**Per-credential allowed IP restrictions**
- `SiteRMLibs/Auth.py`, `SiteFE/REST/Auth.py`, `SiteFE/REST/dependencies.py`: X.509 M2M credentials (DNs) can now be restricted to a set of CIDR ranges via a new `allowed_ips` config entry. Enforced on challenge generation, challenge verification, and token refresh; the real client IP is resolved from `X-Forwarded-For` (falling back to the socket peer) so this works correctly behind a proxy. Credentials without `allowed_ips` configured remain unrestricted.

**Delta requestor information**
- `SiteFE/REST/Delta.py`, `src/html/assets/js/page/deltas.js`: New `GET /api/{sitename}/deltas/{delta_id}/requestinfo` endpoint returns the requestor (name/email/organization/host) and full user-tracking history for a delta. The Web UI delta view now displays this information.

**DOMAIN_COMPONENT DN support**
- `SiteRMLibs/Auth.py`: Added `NameOID.DOMAIN_COMPONENT` (`DC`) to the certificate subject/issuer short-name mapping, so DNs containing DC components are parsed correctly.

**Multiarch / portability improvements**
- `SiteRMAgent/Debugger/Debugger.py`: Falls back to `psutil`-based interface enumeration when the `ip` binary is not available (e.g. non-Linux images).
- `packaging/siterm-site-fe/sitefe.py`: Static UI directory is now configurable via `SITERM_STATIC_DIR`.
- `SiteRMLibs/MainUtilities.py`, `SiteRMLibs/ConfigFetcher.py`: Config file path (`SITERM_CONFIG_FILE`) and config-fetcher failure-counter path (`CONFIG_FETCHER_COUNTER`) are now overridable via env vars; the counter directory is created if missing.
- `SiteRMAgent/RecurringActions/DTNMain.py`: Added `agent.disabled_plugins` config option to skip loading specific recurring-action plugins (CertInfo, KubeInfo, NetInfo, ArpInfo).

**Documentation**
- Added Node Exporter installation and security hardening guides (passthrough via Frontend to avoid exposing `/debug/pprof` on agents) to the installation docs.

### 🐛 Bug Fixes

**Certificate chain verification**
- `SiteRMLibs/Auth.py`, `SiteRMLibs/hostcert.py`: Certificate verification now validates the full chain (leaf + embedded intermediates) instead of the leaf certificate only. Previously, host certificates issued with an intermediate CA could fail chain validation even though the chain was valid.

**Token refresh could be reported as failed after succeeding**
- `SiteRMLibs/HTTPLibrary.py`: Fixed a missing `return` after a successful token refresh; the code could fall through and treat a successful renewal as an error.

**Stale device state never refreshed**
- `SiteFE/LookUpService/lookup.py`: Fixed an inverted time comparison (`>=` instead of `<=`) that prevented the "warnings raised more than 1 hour ago" path from ever triggering a device state refresh.

**System readiness check used OR instead of AND**
- `SiteFE/REST/dependencies.py`: `checkReadyState` now requires both `LookUpService` and `ProvisioningService` to have completed their first run before reporting the API ready, instead of either one.

**Falsy default values ignored in config lookups**
- `SiteRMLibs/GitConfig.py`: `get()` treated any falsy default (`False`, `[]`, `0`) as "no default provided" and raised instead of returning it. Now correctly checks `default is not None`.

**Delta global state default**
- `SiteFE/PolicyService/policyService.py`: Default delta global state changed from `activated` to `deactivated` when no sub-delta states are present.

**Delta submit tracking recorded too late**
- `SiteFE/REST/Delta.py`: The delta `submit` action is now recorded before processing instead of after, so the audit trail is preserved even if processing subsequently fails.

**Database URL construction**
- `SiteRMLibs/DBBackend.py`: Database connection URL is now built via SQLAlchemy's `URL.create()` instead of an f-string, so usernames/passwords containing special characters are correctly escaped.

**Host stats collection hardening**
- `SiteRMLibs/MemDiskStats.py`: Guards against malformed `df` output rows, filesystems missing an `Avail_gb` value, and `psutil.AccessDenied` errors when enumerating processes, instead of raising.

**Misc**
- Removed a stray debug log line that printed raw token content during token validation (`SiteRMLibs/Auth.py`).

### 🔧 Supported OS Releases

- **Frontend (x86_64)**
  - EL9
- **Agent (x86_64)**
  - EL9
  - EL10 **Default for release**
  - U22
- **Debugger (x86_64)**
  - EL10

